{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal-record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about or require disclosure of an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer, and may not consider arrests without conviction, expunged, pardoned, vacated, sealed or juvenile records at any time.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Dwelling units offered for rent for residential purposes, except units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Director may impose monetary penalties of up to $1,000, $5,000 or $10,000 for first, second and third or later violations, and order compliance action.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"C.46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure and refund","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether it reviews criminal history and that the applicant may submit evidence of inaccuracies or rehabilitation; the director may order the fee returned for a violation.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Dwelling units offered for rent for residential purposes, except units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Duty is triggered before a housing provider accepts any application fee","coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Director may require return of the applicant's rental application fee and payment of up to $1,000 to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"C.46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after successful appeal of director's housing order","requirement":"If a housing provider's appeal succeeds and a court overturns the director's order resulting in housing, that determination is grounds to evict the former applicant with at least 45 days' notice.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"A former applicant residing in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director's order.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Applies to a former applicant housed by the director's order whose provider later wins an appeal","coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"C.46:8-63","quoted_span":"shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

